# TODO

Long-running work, in the order chosen. Check items off as they land; keep the notes short.

## 1. Disclosure-time pipeline (active)

The edge is speed from disclosure, so disclosure time is the one timestamp everywhere.

- [x] Live discovery: EDGAR current-filings Atom feed (`action=getcurrent&type=4&owner=only&output=atom`, de-duplicated by accession, exact form match) replaces the Selenium scraper; verified live
- [x] Retire Selenium: remove `EdgarClient.fetch_live_links` / `_configure_driver`, the `edgar-live` extra (selenium, beautifulsoup4) and the Chromium layer of the master-index image; update the `Filings` port
- [x] Single timestamp: the scraper parses `ACCEPTANCE-DATETIME` from each filing header and stamps every transaction with it, in backfill and live mode alike
- [x] master-index: drop `received_now`; discovery (quarterly master index or Atom feed) only selects which filings to fetch
- [x] Scraper age filter compares filing publication times (was a no-op in live mode)
- [x] Look-ahead bias: `compute_target` enters at the first price after acceptance (same-day close in session, next open otherwise), not at the trade date; `compute_RT4` only averages labels whose exit close printed before acceptance; every label changes, so BT4/RT4 are rebuilt
- [ ] Intraday entries: Alpaca minute bars (adapter behind `MarketData`) for a window around each filing; entry = first bar after acceptance plus processing latency; extended hours vs next open for out-of-session filings; spread/slippage and short constraints (borrow, short-sale restriction) in the labels
- [ ] AWS plan: event-driven live path (EventBridge poll -> dedupe -> SQS + DLQ -> scorer Lambda -> Alpaca) beside the batch path (backfill, RT4 labelling, training)

